; Tutorial_7_Statistics_and_Reports.inix -- counts, figures and reports.

[about]
Title=7 - Statistics and Reports
Intro=The numbers in a column with Alt plus Shift plus S, a chart's figures with Control plus Shift plus G, and a report written as a document with Alt plus Shift plus R.
Setup=JobTrail is open in DbDo; Alt plus Shift plus D opens it.
Homework=Run a report of your own table and read it in your browser.

[step]

Say=One want: how many applications, how they stand, and a page to keep.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=I move to the status column. Alt plus Shift plus S, S for Statistics, describes the column.
Key=Alt+Shift+S
Hear=Statistics from Column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The count of each value, and for numbers the sum, average, least and most. Escape closes it.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus G, G for Graphics, turns a column into a chart and its figures in words.
Key=Control+Shift+G
Hear=Graphics Column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Alt plus Shift plus R, R for Report, writes a saved report as a document.
Key=Alt+Shift+R
Hear=Run Report dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose a report and press Enter; DbDo writes it and opens it.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the report's title, as a heading)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: a report reads the whole table, filter or not, unless its template says otherwise. To report only some records, filter them and use the report that respects the filter.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Before the details, the shape. Alt plus T, Table Summary, says how many records and columns the table has, and how much room it takes.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Table Summary
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, and Alt plus D, Database Summary, does the same for every table in the database.
Key=Alt+D
Hear=Database Summary
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A filter narrows a summary to what matters: filter to waiting jobs, then Alt plus Shift plus S again, and the counts describe only those.
Key=Alt+Shift+S
Hear=Statistics from Column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=When the numbers are to go somewhere else, Alt plus X, Export Data, writes the table, or the records in view, as CSV, a spreadsheet, JSON or another format.
Key=Alt+X
Hear=Export Data dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, for now. And Control plus P prints the records in view, for a copy on paper or a PDF.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A single number is often all that is wanted. Control plus C copies the cell under the cursor.
Key=Control+C
Hear=Copied
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus C appends another cell to what is on the clipboard, to gather a few figures in one go.
Key=Alt+C
Hear=Appended
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Apostrophe, Say Clipboard, reads back what has been gathered before it is pasted anywhere.
Key=Alt+Apostrophe
Hear=12, waiting 4
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Then one paste puts those figures in an email or a document.
Key=

[step]

Say=Before reading any summary, Shift plus 8 says the sort and filter in force, since both change what the numbers describe.
Key=Shift+8
Hear=Sort: employer. Filter: none.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And Alt plus L reads a whole column aloud, top to bottom, when hearing the values beats counting them.
Key=Alt+L
Hear=waiting, applied, interview, waiting
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Describe a column.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus S

[step]

Say=A column as a chart.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus G

[step]

Say=Run a report.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus R
